r."],["SPAN",{},["STRONG",{"style":"color: rgb(134, 239, 172);"},"✓ Exact analysis (Method of Joints). "],"Forces are computed from 2D pin-jointed equilibrium: for each joint, sum of forces in x and sum of forces in y both equal zero. ","The resulting linear system (26 equations, 26 unknowns) is solved by Gaussian elimination with partial pivoting. Hover over any member in the diagram to see its exact tension or compression force. The maximum chord force (0 kN) and maximum diagonal force (0 kN) are now the actual peak member forces, not deep-beam approximations."]]]]]]],[[4,20]],[[4,21]],[[4,22]],[[4,23]],[[4,24]],[[4,25]],[[4,26]],[[4,27]]]],"viewport":{"width":1000,"height":900},"timestamp":413566.15,"wallTime":1790654305146,"collectionTime":29.699999999720603,"resourceOverrides":[],"isMainFrame":true}}
