{"type":"after","callId":"call@946","endTime":414870.577,"result":{"matches":false,"received":{"value":{"s":"Compare wood, structural steel and FRP sections against the chosen strength and buckling margin. Geometry and loads use your current settings. Stone, cast iron and reinforced concrete are excluded because this simple axial model does not represent their tensile or reinforcement behavior.Positions to optimizeWhole crossingCurrent positionEvery vehicle position is covered by the force extremes at the load-transfer joints. Applying a design also runs and saves its crossing test.Target safety factor2.01.5 (very thin margin)2.0 (learning target)4.0+ (conservative)6.0 (Brooklyn Bridge)✓ 68 combinations pass. Top 5 by cost:RankMaterialCross-sectionSF yieldSF bucklingMassCost (USD)🏆 1Structural Steel8,500 mm²17.002.159775 kg$586512Structural Steel9,000 mm²18.002.4110350 kg$621013FRP Composite (fiber-reinforced polymer)18,500 mm²63.432.035420 kg$650454Structural Steel9,500 mm²19.002.6810925 kg$655515FRP Composite (fiber-reinforced polymer)19,000 mm²65.142.155567 kg$66803Note: Cost estimate is material-only — doesn't include labor, fabrication, transport, fastening, or maintenance over the bridge's lifetime. Real bridge economics also factor in durability (steel maintenance vs concrete) + replacement cycle. But raw material cost is the starting line.Click the winner: Apply this design to my bridge"},"ariaSnapshot":"- paragraph: Compare wood, structural steel and FRP sections against the chosen strength and buckling margin. Geometry and loads use your current settings. Stone, cast iron and reinforced concrete are excluded because this simple axial model does not represent their tensile or reinforcement behavior.\n- text: Positions to optimize\n- combobox \"Positions to optimize\":\n  - option \"Whole crossing\" [selected]\n  - option \"Current position\"\n- paragraph: Every vehicle position is covered by the force extremes at the load-transfer joints. Applying a design also runs and saves its crossing test.\n- text: Target safety factor 2.0\n- slider \"Target safety factor\": \"2\"\n- text: \"1.5 (very thin margin) 2.0 (learning target) 4.0+ (conservative) 6.0 (Brooklyn Bridge) ✓ 68 combinations pass. Top 5 by cost:\"\n- region \"Top bridge designs by cost\":\n  - table:\n    - rowgroup:\n      - row \"Rank Material Cross-section SF yield SF buckling Mass Cost (USD)\":\n        - columnheader \"Rank\"\n        - columnheader \"Material\"\n        - columnheader \"Cross-section\"\n        - columnheader \"SF yield\"\n        - columnheader \"SF buckling\"\n        - columnheader \"Mass\"\n        - columnheader \"Cost (USD)\"\n    - rowgroup:\n      - row \"🏆 1 Structural Steel 8,500 mm² 17.00 2.15 9775 kg $58651\":\n        - cell \"🏆 1\"\n        - cell \"Structural Steel\"\n        - cell \"8,500 mm²\"\n        - cell \"17.00\"\n        - cell \"2.15\"\n        - cell \"9775 kg\"\n        - cell \"$58651\"\n      - row \"2 Structural Steel 9,000 mm² 18.00 2.41 10350 kg $62101\":\n        - cell \"2\"\n        - cell \"Structural Steel\"\n        - cell \"9,000 mm²\"\n        - cell \"18.00\"\n        - cell \"2.41\"\n        - cell \"10350 kg\"\n        - cell \"$62101\"\n      - row \"3 FRP Composite (fiber-reinforced polymer) 18,500 mm² 63.43 2.03 5420 kg $65045\":\n        - cell \"3\"\n        - cell \"FRP Composite (fiber-reinforced polymer)\"\n        - cell \"18,500 mm²\"\n        - cell \"63.43\"\n        - cell \"2.03\"\n        - cell \"5420 kg\"\n        - cell \"$65045\"\n      - row \"4 Structural Steel 9,500 mm² 19.00 2.68 10925 kg $65551\":\n        - cell \"4\"\n        - cell \"Structural Steel\"\n        - cell \"9,500 mm²\"\n        - cell \"19.00\"\n        - cell \"2.68\"\n        - cell \"10925 kg\"\n        - cell \"$65551\"\n      - row \"5 FRP Composite (fiber-reinforced polymer) 19,000 mm² 65.14 2.15 5567 kg $66803\":\n        - cell \"5\"\n        - cell \"FRP Composite (fiber-reinforced polymer)\"\n        - cell \"19,000 mm²\"\n        - cell \"65.14\"\n        - cell \"2.15\"\n        - cell \"5567 kg\"\n        - cell \"$66803\"\n- strong: \"Note:\"\n- text: Cost estimate is material-only — doesn't include labor, fabrication, transport, fastening, or maintenance over the bridge's lifetime. Real bridge economics also factor in durability (steel maintenance vs concrete) + replacement cycle. But raw material cost is the starting line.\n- strong: \"Click the winner:\"\n- button \"Apply this design to my bridge\""}},"afterSnapshot":"after@call@946"}
