{"type":"after","callId":"call@1056","endTime":428202.141,"result":{"matches":true,"received":{"value":{"s":"Crossing investigationwarren · 36 m × 6 m · 6 bays · Structural Steel · 8500 mm²120 kN at 1% of span · bracing every 1 panelsSAFE · SF 17.90 · $58651Saved crossing: SF 2.15 at 8.3% of span; buckling. 57 tested positions.Same span and applied load. Current material cost change: +$0Prediction: I predict that a thicker section will improve the buckling margin because bending stiffness increases.Observation: The whole crossing met the target. A diagonal changed from tension to compression as the vehicle moved.RestoreRemove"},"ariaSnapshot":"- article:\n  - heading \"Crossing investigation\" [level=4]\n  - paragraph: warren · 36 m × 6 m · 6 bays · Structural Steel · 8500 mm²\n  - paragraph: 120 kN at 1% of span · bracing every 1 panels\n  - strong: SAFE · SF 17.90 · $58651\n  - paragraph: \"Saved crossing: SF 2.15 at 8.3% of span; buckling. 57 tested positions.\"\n  - paragraph: \"Same span and applied load. Current material cost change: +$0\"\n  - paragraph:\n    - strong: \"Prediction:\"\n    - text: I predict that a thicker section will improve the buckling margin because bending stiffness increases.\n  - paragraph:\n    - strong: \"Observation:\"\n    - text: The whole crossing met the target. A diagonal changed from tension to compression as the vehicle moved.\n  - button \"Restore Crossing investigation\": Restore\n  - button \"Remove Crossing investigation\": Remove"}},"afterSnapshot":"after@call@1056"}
